cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use neurOS or ORION in research, cite the exact release tag or commit used so the software and evidence boundary are reproducible."
title: "neurOS: neural execution, interoperability, and evidence infrastructure"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hulyalkar
    given-names: Sidharth
repository-code: "https://github.com/sidhulyalkar/neurOS-v1"
url: "https://github.com/sidhulyalkar/neurOS-v1"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - brain-computer interface
  - neuroscience
  - neural decoding
  - neural interfaces
  - neuroai
  - reproducibility
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - neural representation
abstract: >-
  neurOS is an open execution and evidence platform for neural interfaces.
  It provides explicit neural data, timing, runtime, recording/replay,
  interoperability, qualification, and provenance contracts. ORION is the
  complementary neural-intelligence plane for tokenization, learned
  representations, transfer, personalization, and auditable adaptation.
